From d6c0707508f03ad74578b514ac01cba020335af4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:36:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: the SAM/PIC32CM frequency meter (FREQM U2257)

mchp-freqm counts GCLK_FREQM_MSR (its "gclk") over REFNUM periods of
GCLK_FREQM_REF (a new clock input, "gclk-ref"), both wired from the
device's GCLK_ID_MSR/GCLK_ID_REF channels, as three probe rounds on
PIC32CM MC00 rev A1 silicon showed (firmware/hello APP=freqmprobe):
VALUE = REFNUM * f_MSR / f_REF with no bias, REFNUM 0 counting as 512,
a window of REFNUM + 2.5 reference periods with the live count in VALUE,
a 24-bit wrap with OVF (cleared by disabling), DONE whatever INTENSET
says, START ignored while busy or disabled, an abort on disable, a wait
for a missing reference clock. One model for the JH01, MC00 and SAM E51.

The GCLK generators now multiply their source's period instead of
dividing integer Hz, so every divider is exact (48 MHz / 2^17 was 366
Hz, and FREQM read 0xFE4B3E where silicon reads 0xFE0000).
mchp_regblock_set_clock_period() sets a clock by period. qtest
pic32cm-freqm-test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
